mullion is built from three open-source projects, altered so that they share
one event loop, together with the code written for it. This notice names each
project, its licence, the commit merged and where its code lives in this tree.

The zlib licence on go-shirei requires that the origin of the software is not
misrepresented, and that an altered version is plainly marked as such and not
presented as the original. Every directory below that came from another
project is an altered version of it, and carries an ALTERED.md saying how it
differs from the commit merged and which files were changed or added.

The code written for mullion is under the MIT licence in LICENSE: the root
package (mullion.go, window.go, nativewindow.go, openurl.go and their tests,
binaries_test.go, ffiaudit_test.go), bind/, dialog/, icon/, examples/,
internal/brand/, internal/mainthread/, internal/objc/ and internal/win32/, and
the files each ALTERED.md lists as added for mullion. internal/mainthread,
internal/objc and internal/win32 replace helpers that each of the three
projects carried for itself: pinning the main thread and posting work to it, an
Objective-C selector and class cache, and the Win32 window and menu bindings.

